----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = key
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Key Field**
C D
C D This is the primary identifier for ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} instances. Key fields:
C D - Must be unique within their scope
C D - Used for lookup and indexing
C D - Cannot be empty or duplicated
C D - Become the search key when ${.gen_element_guide.parent.find} is specified
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = word
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Word Field**
C D
C D Single whitespace-delimited token. Word fields:
C D - Cannot contain spaces or special characters
C D - Read until first whitespace
C D - Suitable for identifiers, flags, enums
C D - Access via: `$\{${name}\}` in actors
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = text
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Text Field**
C D
C D Free-form text extending to end of line. Text fields:
C D - Can contain spaces and special characters
C D - Read from current position to line end
C D - Suitable for descriptions, documentation, expressions
C D - Access via: `$\{${name}\}` in actors
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = number
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Number Field**
C D
C D Numeric value field. Number fields:
C D - Stores integer or floating-point values
C D - Used for counts, indices, measurements
C D - Can be used in calculations
C D - Access via: `$\{${name}\}` in actors
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = ref
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Reference (ref)**
C D
C D Global reference to a ${comp:c} component. Reference fields:
C D - Look up ${comp:c} instances by their key field
C D - Target must be globally searchable (`Find`)
C D - Resolved by name during multi-pass loading
C D - Creates K${name:l}p (integer pointer) internally
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access target fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** First pass - looks up "${comp:c}" in global index by the value in this field.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = link
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Link (sibling reference)**
C D
C D Sibling reference within same parent. Link fields:
C D - Look up ${comp:c} instances within current parent's children
C D - Both this component and ${comp:c} share the same parent type
C D - Target must be indexed within parent (`FindIn`)
C D - Resolved during loading, creates K${name:l}p pointer
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access target fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** First pass - looks up sibling ${comp:c} by name within parent's child index.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = ref_copy
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Reference Copy (ref_copy)**
C D
C D Copies a reference from a previous field. Reference copy fields:
C D - Duplicates the resolved pointer from an earlier ref/link element
C D - Previous element must point to same ${comp:c} component type
C D - Enables reference reuse without re-resolving
C D - Useful for reference chains and shared targets
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access target fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** Second pass - copies the K*p pointer from the previous element that references ${comp:c}.
C D **Requirement:** A preceding element in this component must be a ref/link/ref_copy to ${comp:c}.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = ref_child
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Child Reference (ref_child)**
C D
C D Lookup child within previously referenced component. Child reference fields:
C D - Looks up ${comp:c} child inside component referenced by previous field
C D - Creates parent→child lookup chain
C D - Previous element establishes parent context
C D - This field's value is the child's key name
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access target fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** Second+ pass - uses previous element's resolved component as search context, looks up ${comp:c} child by name.
C D **Requirement:** Previous element must resolve to a component that has ${comp:c} children.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = up_copy
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Up-Chain Copy (up_copy)**
C D
C D Navigate up parent hierarchy to find ancestor. Up-chain fields:
C D - Walks parent pointers until ${comp:c} ancestor found
C D - Sets context for subsequent ref_child lookups
C D - No value needed in data file (computed automatically)
C D - Enables upward traversal in nested hierarchies
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access ancestor fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** Second+ pass - traverses parent chain: current→parent→grandparent... until ${comp:c} type found.
C D **Usage:** Typically followed by ref_child to look up children within the found ancestor.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = type_of
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Type-Of Reference**
C D
C D Reference child by component type name. Type-of fields:
C D - Field value is a component type name (e.g., "Op", "Layer")
C D - Finds child whose component type matches the value
C D - Different from ref_child which matches by key field
C D - Enables polymorphic component references
C D - Navigate via: `Its ${name:l} actor`
C D - Access target fields: `$\{${name:l}.field_name\}`
C D
C D **Resolution:** Matches child component where kComp type name equals this field's value.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element type = tree
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: Tree Level**
C D
C D Numeric depth value for hierarchical navigation. Tree fields:
C D - Stores integer level/depth in hierarchy
C D - Enables special tree traversal commands
C D - Navigate up: `Its ${name:l}.up actor`
C D - Navigate down: `Its ${name:l}.down actor`
C D - Navigate left: `Its ${name:l}.left actor` (previous sibling)
C D - Navigate right: `Its ${name:l}.right actor` (next sibling)
C D
C D **Usage:** Typically used for outline levels, indentation depths, or tree structures.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_desc Element .
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Type: ${type}**
C D
C D Custom or extension type.
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type in key,word,text,number
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} <${type}_value>
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = ref
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} <${comp:l}_key>  # Must match existing ${comp:c} key
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
C D ${name} target_${comp:l}  # References ${comp:c} with key "target_${comp:l}"
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = link
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} <sibling_${comp:l}_key>  # Sibling ${comp:c} under same parent
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.parent.name:c} parent_instance
C D   ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
C D   ${name} other_instance  # Links to sibling ${comp:c}
C D   ${comp:c} other_instance
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = ref_copy
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D <previous_ref_to_${comp:c}> <target>
C D ${name} .  # Copies reference from above (no value needed)
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
C D base_ref target_${comp:l}  # First reference to ${comp:c}
C D ${name} .  # Copies the same reference
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = ref_child
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D <parent_ref> <parent_key>  # Establishes parent context
C D ${name} <child_key>  # Child ${comp:c} key within parent
C D ```
C D
C D **Real Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
Its .gen_element_guide.parent.Element gen_show_prev_ref
C D ${name} ${comp:l}_child  # Finds ${comp:c} child within the referenced component
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_show_prev_ref Element type in ref,link,up_copy
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D ${name} parent_instance  # References parent

Break loop

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = up_copy
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} .  # No value needed - computed automatically
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
C D ${name} .  # Finds ${comp:c} ancestor automatically
C D next_field child_key  # Can now look up children in that ancestor
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = type_of
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} <ComponentType>  # Name of component type (e.g., "Op", "SamplingOp")
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} my_instance
C D ${name} SamplingOp  # Finds child of type "SamplingOp"
C D ```
C D

----------------------------------------------------------------
Actor gen_type_usage Element type = tree
----------------------------------------------------------------

C D
C D **Data File Format:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} <key_value>
C D ${name} <level_number>  # Integer depth/level (e.g., 2, 3, 4)
C D ```
C D
C D **Example:**
C D ```
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} section_1
C D ${name} 2  # Level 2 heading
C D 
C D ${.gen_element_guide.parent.name:c} section_1_1
C D ${name} 3  # Level 3 heading (child)
C D ```
C D

